 ## Endpoints
 
-- `GET /items` → `{"items": [...]}`: every item, ordered by `id`.
+- `GET /items?limit=<1..100>&cursor=<opaque>` → `{"items": [...], "next_cursor": "..."}`: items ordered by `id`, with a default limit of 20. Follow `next_cursor` unchanged to fetch the next page; it is `null` on the last page. Invalid limits or cursors return HTTP-shaped status 400 and `{"error": "..."}`.
 - `GET /items/<id>` → the item, 404 when unknown, 400 when `id` is not a number.
 
 Run the tests with `python3 -m unittest`.
